# What the build context does not need.
#
# The Dockerfile copies five things by name: the two lock files, pyproject.toml,
# the licence and readme the build reads, and the package itself. Everything
# else here is either large, wrong for the target platform, or both.

# A Windows virtual environment, which is both the largest thing in the
# checkout and useless inside a Linux image.
.venv/
venv/
env/

.git/
.github/
.gitignore

# The suite runs in CI against the source tree, not against the image.
tests/

# Prose and tooling that the image has no use for.
scripts/
CHANGELOG.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md

# Build leftovers. An egg-info from a local editable install names paths that
# do not exist in the image.
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
